   "subject": "Re: Effect of Occasion Length on Estimated Denstiy",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Matt<br><br>If you are fitting a Poisson count model then lumping of occasions is safe, as you suggest. One could check this by looking at the likelihood, but there&#39;s an example below with a simulated dataset that is fairly convincing. Count data clearly contain more information than the same data reduced to binary - a point made also for binomial counts in App A of our 2009 &#39;pattern&#39; paper.<br><br>I&#39;m not aware of evidence that sparseness (number of detections per occasion) is a \r\nproblem in itself (what matters is the total number of individuals and \r\nredetections).<br><br>Notice that I used detectfn = &#39;HHN&#39; (halfnormal on the hazard scale). I haven&#39;t recently tested &#39;HN&#39; etc.<br><br>Collapsing occasions of course limits your ability to model temporal change in lambda0 etc., but in my experience that is seldom a problem.<br><br>Murray<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>grid </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">grid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">nx </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> ny </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">8</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detector </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;count&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">capthist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">grid</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> popn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> buffer </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">100</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Ndist</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;fixed&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;HHN&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> noccasions </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">26</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> seed </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">12349</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                   detectpar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">lambda0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.002</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sigma </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">20</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## The raw data are very sparse at the level of daily &#39;occasions&#39;, even when we sum</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## across detectors:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>table</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># 0    1 </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># 5929   77 </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## now collapse by week, by fortnight, or entire survey:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH7 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reduce</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH14 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reduce</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">CHall</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reduce</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;all&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## the numbers of detections and individuals are unaffected:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>summary</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">CHall</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>fit1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;HHN&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> biasLimit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit7 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;HHN&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> biasLimit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit14 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;HHN&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> biasLimit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitall </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#606\">CHall</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectfn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;HHN&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> biasLimit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NA</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> trace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fits </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secrlist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit7 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit7</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit14 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fit14</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fitall </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fitall</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## estimates of density are the same except for slight numerical effects</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># $fit1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># link estimate SE.estimate      lcl     ucl</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># D        log  9.90150    1.888975  6.83535 14.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># lambda0  log  0.00241    0.000498  0.00161  0.0036</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># sigma    log 20.87248    1.913921 17.44559 24.9725</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># $fit7</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># link estimate SE.estimate     lcl     ucl</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># D        log   9.9015     1.88897  6.8353 14.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># lambda0  log   0.0175     0.00362  0.0117  0.0262</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># sigma    log  20.8725     1.91392 17.4456 24.9725</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># $fit14</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># link estimate SE.estimate     lcl     ucl</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># D        log   9.9015     1.88898  6.8354 14.3431</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># lambda0  log   0.0337     0.00697  0.0226  0.0503</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># sigma    log  20.8725     1.91392 17.4456 24.9725</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># $fitall</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># link estimate SE.estimate      lcl     ucl</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># D        log  9.90146    1.888970  6.83532 14.3430</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># lambda0  log  0.00241    0.000498  0.00161  0.0036</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># sigma    log 20.87249    1.913924 17.44560 24.9725</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## However, the estimate of lambda0 varies for weekly and fortnightly intervals.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## The agreement between the daily and all-occasion lambda0-hat is due to a quirk of</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## reduce.capthist: a usage attribute is constructed when by = &quot;all&quot;; the usage matrix </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## has effort 26 x 7 = 182 at each detector and the fitted lambda0-hat is scaled to a</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## daily value (unless you set ignoreusage).</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## Collapsing the data to a single occasion is much faster (using secr 3.0.3 on a slowish laptop)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fits</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;[[&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;proctime&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># fit1.elapsed   fit7.elapsed  fit14.elapsed fitall.elapsed </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># 1208.42         151.25          58.97          20.49 </span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br> </div>"
    ]
   ]
